{number: 50}
{title: Have Thine Own Way, Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [G7] way!
Thou art the Potter,
I am the [C] clay.
Mould me and [C7] make me
After Thy [F] will,
While I am [C] waiting,
[G7] Yielded and [C] still.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [G7] way!
Search me and try me,
Master, to-[C] day!
Whiter than [C7] snow, Lord,
Wash me just [F] now,
As in Thy [C] presence
[G7] Humbly I [C] bow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [G7] way!
Wounded and weary,
Help me, I [C] pray.
Power, all [C7] power
Surely is [F] Thine!
Touch me and [C] heal me,
[G7] Savior di-[C] vine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [G7] way!
Hold o'er my being
Absolute [C] sway!
Fill with Thy [C7] Spirit
Till all shall [F] see
Christ only, [C] always,
[G7] Living in [C] me!
{end_of_verse}
